                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">The output that matters</p>
                        <h2>A structured digital record, not a stack of paper certificates.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Most field compliance in South Africa still ends in a paper pad, a photo dumped in a phone gallery, or a form typed up back at the office hours later. Quickler changes the output. As a field worker answers over WhatsApp, the work becomes a live record on a dashboard the office can see straight away.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Every answer, photo and voice note lands against the right line item in real time</li>
                        <li>Each item is graded red, amber or green, so a manager sees faults at a glance</li>
                        <li>The record is machine-readable, so it can be searched, filtered and reported on</li>
                        <li>A PDF certificate exports from that same record when a client or regulator needs a document</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The dashboard is the product; the PDF is a convenience on top of it. That is the difference between a record you can manage a business from and a folder of scanned forms.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
