                        <h2>Built for how South African field teams actually work.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>South Africa runs a large, spread-out field-services economy: electrical and solar installers, plumbing and HVAC crews, security and facilities firms, mining contractors, fleet operators, construction site teams and lone workers covering wide areas. WhatsApp is already the default way these teams communicate.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Field workers use the WhatsApp account on their own phone, with nothing new to issue</li>
                        <li>No rugged tablets or kiosks to ship to remote sites, mines or farms</li>
                        <li>Text, voice note or photo all work, so a worker is never blocked by a form</li>
                        <li>One dashboard pulls every job back to a head office in Johannesburg, Cape Town, Durban or anywhere else</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Quickler is rooted in UK compliance work, but it is built to work anywhere WhatsApp does, and South African field firms fit that shape closely.</p>
